Goal: To identify the specific mutation responsible for the visible miniature phenotype in Drosophila melanogaster and understand how that mutation leads to the observed physical changes.
Step 1: Upload the DNA sequence file (.ab1) to the Sabine terminal using scp so it can be accessed and analyzed during the bioinformatics workflow. 
-- This was done on the MacBook terminal using: scp MUT-G44.ab1 pcshedr2@sabine.rcdc.uh.edu:/project/stuckert/pcshedr2/Final_Project/
Step 2: Convert the .ab1 files to FASTA files
-- I used Biopython as it can read .ab1 files directly and convert them to FASTA. 
---- Biopython was not installed on my terminal, so I installed it with: python -m pip install --user biopython (output: successfully installed biopython-1.85)
-- Now, to convert the .ab1 file to FASTA, the following command was used: python -c "from Bio import SeqIO; SeqIO.convert('MUT-G44.ab1', 'abi', 'miniature.fasta', 'fasta')"
-- I used dos2unix to convert Windows-style line endings (CRLF) into Unix-style line endings (LF), which helps when files are transferred between systems. 

